//! Product requirements, feature contracts and architecture decisions.

#[doc = "# Mealshop\n\nRecipes, informed nutrition, shopping and family meal planning. **Early bootstrap:** only a\nRust HTTP server with `GET /health` exists. All product features below are planned.\n\n[![CI](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n[![Audit](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/workflows/audit.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/workflows/audit.yml)\n[Documentation](https://th3link.github.io/mealshop/) · [Feature specs](../page_specs_readme_md/index.html) ·\n[Requirements](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html) · [ADRs](../page_docs_adr_index_md/index.html)\n\n## Vision\n- Ingredient database, precise configurable units, scalable recipes, macro- and micronutrients\n  per serving, and evidence-backed explanations of beneficial food components.\n- Shared recipes and later paid recipes/collections; source-link-only sharing for imported recipes.\n- Shopping lists with recipe provenance, extra items, preferred shops, learned aisle order and barcodes.\n- Family meal plans with attendance, intolerances, preferences, cooking time and ongoing feedback.\n- Guided cooking with preset timers, multi-day bread/pizza schedules, and later brewing/fermentation.\n- Inventory, offers, customer-operated link imports and MCP recipe tools.\n\n## Run the bootstrap\nInstall stable Rust (declared minimum: 1.85), then:\n```sh\ncargo run --locked\ncurl --fail http://127.0.0.1:3000/health\n```\nThe response is `ok` plus a newline. `MEALSHOP_LISTEN_ADDR` overrides `127.0.0.1:3000`.\nUse Ctrl-C for graceful shutdown. No authentication, storage or recipe endpoints exist yet;\nthis is a development stub. Tests: `cargo test --locked`. Full gate: [development guide](../page_docs_guides_development_md/index.html).\n\n## Deployment and business model (planned)\nRust/Tokio/Axum server, standalone or as a Nextcloud `ExApp`; Flutter client connecting to an\nown server or our hosted service. Storage options: Git-backed files, PostgreSQL, SQLite and\nMariaDB. Nextcloud installations remain free. Hosted accounts have free and paid tiers.\nThe distributed app costs a few euros; self-compilation and installation remain possible.\nOnly paid, signed app releases are intended to connect to our operated service; technical\nadmission and licensing details need validation (ADR 0004). Future federation may exchange\nrecipes and compatible meal plans between independent servers.\n\n## Contribute\nStart with [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/blob/main/AGENTS.md), the [roadmap](../page_docs_roadmap_md/index.html) and an affected feature spec.\nThe repository uses spec-driven development inspired by Curvyo and CI adapted from\nhomeautomation; exact source revisions and adaptation notes are in [provenance](../page_docs_provenance_md/index.html).\n\n## License\nAGPL-3.0-only. See [LICENSE](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/blob/main/LICENSE). Paid distribution does not remove recipients' rights\nto use, modify or redistribute the software under that licence.\n"]
pub mod page_readme_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0001: stack and delivery\n\nStatus: Accepted for bootstrap; future integrations planned\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nThe customer requests Rust/Axum, a Flutter app, Nextcloud `ExApp` deployment and the homeautomation CI baseline.\n\n## Decision\nUse a single Rust package with Tokio/Axum and a small reusable router plus executable. Declare Rust 1.85 (edition 2024 baseline) and verify it in CI. Ship only /health now. Publish embedded project docs through rustdoc and Pages. Adapt the upstream workflows to a host binary, keeping build, coverage, MSRV, SPDX SBOM, audit, licences, Renovate and size metrics.\n\n## Alternatives\nSeparate crates now would add unused boundaries. A different backend or frontend stack would contradict the request.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nFlutter, Nextcloud `AppAPI` authentication and packaging need later integration specs. A healthy process is not proof of database readiness. Metrics are binary size, not latency or nutrition accuracy.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0001_stack_and_delivery_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0002: quantities and nutrition\n\nStatus: Proposed implementation; customer unit preferences accepted\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nRecipes accept varied input while the customer wants only grams/kilograms in personal views. Nutrition and educational effects require provenance.\n\n## Decision\nRetain exact decimal input and unit, dimension, source and conversion context. Normalize mass to grams, volume to millilitres and counts to pieces within their own dimensions. Convert across dimensions only with ingredient/state-specific density or piece mass. Keep serving scaling rational/decimal until display. Persist source values and conversion versions for reproducibility. Nutrition per serving includes units, reference basis, source, missingness and uncertainty. Educational component notes carry evidence and conditions.\n\n## Alternatives\nStoring everything as grams loses volume/count meaning and needs unavailable densities. Bare binary floating point and universal teaspoon conversions obscure precision. Preserve-only-without-normalization complicates aggregation.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nNumeric library/scale, regional spoon standards, nutrient provider and cooking retention factors are unresolved. No conversion is fabricated. Display preferences never rewrite recipe source data.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0003: persistence and data boundaries\n\nStatus: Customer storage targets accepted; schema and adapters proposed\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nThe same household data must work in Git/files, PostgreSQL, SQLite and MariaDB, standalone or in Nextcloud.\n\n## Decision\nDefine versioned domain records with stable identities, explicit provenance, household ownership and recipe revisions before an adapter. Implement adapters incrementally with shared behavioural fixtures. Keep Git history/merge semantics separate from SQL transactions. Require backup/export/import validation and conflict handling. Do not select an ORM or create a generic repository trait in the bootstrap.\n\n## Alternatives\nSQL-only would exclude Git/files. A single SQL dialect assumed across all engines is unverified. Git does not substitute for authorization or concurrent-write control.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nFirst adapter, offline sync, encryption, attachment storage and transaction boundaries need feature-level design. Plans/purchases/stock movements must not silently overwrite one another.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0003_persistence_and_data_boundaries_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0004: licensing hosting and sharing\n\nStatus: AGPL and business goals accepted; admission/commerce/federation proposed\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nThe customer requests AGPL-3.0 software, free Nextcloud installations, paid official app distribution, optional self-builds, hosted tiers and later paid content/federation.\n\n## Decision\nLicense project code AGPL-3.0-only with complete source. Treat app purchase/hosted service entitlement as service policy, separate from software rights. Validate platform attestation plus server-side account entitlement before implementing official-client admission; never rely on a secret in an open client. Preserve source-link-only sharing on every output path for imported recipes. Purchased recipe content needs a separate explicit content licence and provenance. Federation is opt-in and later.\n\n## Alternatives\nObscuring source or prohibiting AGPL redistribution conflicts with the stated licence. A signature alone does not establish account payment or prevent all custom clients. Republishing imported content contradicts the customer sharing restriction.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nPlatform feasibility, AGPL compliance of admission terms, content rights, refunds/tax and federation trust remain gates before commercial launch. No restriction on self-hosting or self-building is introduced by this bootstrap.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0004_licensing_hosting_and_sharing_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0005: privacy and learning\n\nStatus: Proposed safeguards for customer-requested learning\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nMeal planning combines household attendance, dietary constraints, ratings and shopping behaviour. These can reveal sensitive personal information.\n\n## Decision\nScope records and MCP tools to authorized households. Separate hard exclusions from soft preferences; unknown allergen data needs review. Store check-off/cooking/rating events with correction and deletion support. Start from explainable rules; evaluate opt-in incremental learning against that baseline. Keep manual overrides, history reset and opt-out. Calendar and external lookups disclose what leaves the server and request appropriate consent.\n\n## Alternatives\nUnconstrained collaborative training could expose health information or override exclusions. Cold-start ML alone has no useful evidence. Silent calendar writes exceed the request.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nAuthentication, retention, model choice, external APIs and consent UX remain open. Imported text/remote MCP content is untrusted data, not executable instructions.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0005_privacy_and_learning_md {}

#[doc = "# ADR 0006: durable process schedules\n\nStatus: Proposed shared process model\nDate: 2026-11-07\n\n## Context\nCooking, multi-day dough and brewing need timers, dependencies, phase reminders and equipment-specific variants.\n\n## Decision\nModel a process instance as versioned steps with dependencies, active/passive durations, target windows, equipment and persisted deadlines/completion. A server scheduler dispatches idempotent reminders with acknowledgement state. Clients show delivery limits and recover deadlines on reconnect. Preview downstream effects when delays or target times change. Store absolute instants with intended local timezone for civil-time scheduling.\n\n## Alternatives\nA transient in-app countdown cannot survive restarts or multi-day schedules. A separate scheduler per food type duplicates dependency logic. Automatic equipment control is beyond the request.\n\n## Consequences and open questions\nNotification providers, offline authority, retries and daylight-saving semantics need tests. Fermentation duration and notification delivery remain uncertain; no guaranteed outcome or safety claim.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_adr_0006_durable_process_schedules_md {}

#[doc = "# Architecture decisions\n\nUse the next free four-digit number. Record context, alternatives, decision, consequences\nand status; supersede accepted decisions explicitly rather than silently rewriting history.\nA proposal is not customer acceptance of an unresolved choice.\n\n- [ADR 0001: stack and delivery](../page_docs_adr_0001_stack_and_delivery_md/index.html) — Accepted for bootstrap; future integrations planned.\n- [ADR 0002: quantities and nutrition](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html) — Proposed implementation; customer unit preferences accepted.\n- [ADR 0003: persistence and data boundaries](../page_docs_adr_0003_persistence_and_data_boundaries_md/index.html) — Customer storage targets accepted; schema and adapters proposed.\n- [ADR 0004: licensing hosting and sharing](../page_docs_adr_0004_licensing_hosting_and_sharing_md/index.html) — AGPL and business goals accepted; admission/commerce/federation proposed.\n- [ADR 0005: privacy and learning](../page_docs_adr_0005_privacy_and_learning_md/index.html) — Proposed safeguards for customer-requested learning.\n- [ADR 0006: durable process schedules](../page_docs_adr_0006_durable_process_schedules_md/index.html) — Proposed shared process model.\n"]
