#[doc = "# Bootstrap verification\n\nDate: 2026-11-07. Bootstrap source commit: `2a2ad812fd33992fba0e48c66fdd1e4291e3dfd3`.\nThe follow-up commit only records completion/evidence and regenerates the embedded docs.\n\n## Local acceptance evidence\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`: PASS.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 4 passed, 0 skipped. Health returns 200 and\n  exactly `ok\\n`; unknown recipes route returns 404; invalid address and occupied port fail startup.\n- `cargo build --release --locked`: PASS.\n- `cargo deny check licenses`: PASS; no upstream licence exceptions copied.\n- `cargo audit`: PASS, 1,422 `RustSec` advisories loaded; no advisory exceptions.\n- `cargo msrv verify -- cargo check --all-targets --locked`: PASS on Rust 1.85.0.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked`: PASS.\n- `python3 scripts/generate_docs.py --check`: PASS.\n- SPDX JSON generation: 54 packages including the server and dependency graph.\n- Real TCP smoke check with a custom listen address: HTTP 200/body verified; Ctrl-C exits 0.\n- All 75 generated rustdoc project pages checked for missing local file links: none.\n- Published Pages landing page fetched successfully over HTTPS.\n\n## Manually dispatched GitHub workflows\nAll four completed with conclusion **success** against the bootstrap source commit:\n\n| Workflow | Evidence | Coverage |\n|---|---|---|\n| CI | [Run 42367613245](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/runs/42367613245) | fmt, clippy, nextest/coverage, MSRV, debug/release builds, SPDX SBOM, binary metrics |\n| Security audit | [Run 42367615043](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/runs/42367615043) | `RustSec` advisories and licence policy |\n| Docs | [Run 42367617179](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/runs/42367617179) | strict rustdoc, Pages artifact and deployment |\n| Renovate | [Run 42367619146](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/actions/runs/42367619146) | existing repository token, scan and update PR creation |\n\nThe first push-triggered CI was superseded by the manual CI through the configured concurrency\npolicy. The manual run completed all six jobs successfully. Artifacts include debug/release\nLinux `x86_64` executables, coverage, SPDX SBOM, per-profile metrics and the combined metrics report.\nMetrics currently measure binary bytes and are stored as per-run artifacts; firmware memory\nbudgets/history from the ESP project are not applicable to this server bootstrap.\n\nRenovate created update PRs for `actions/configure-pages` and `actions/deploy-pages`.\nThose are separate dependency changes, not silently merged into the bootstrap.\n\n## Delivered scope\n20 feature contracts, six ADRs, README, contributor guidance, roadmap, full AGPL-3.0 text,\nTokio/Axum stub and four workflows. Only F01 is Done; F02–F20 remain Draft.\nThis verifies a delivery foundation, not production readiness of the planned product.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_bootstrap_verification_md {}

#[doc = "# Development and delivery\n\nStart with AGENTS.md and the affected spec. Use stable Rust; Cargo.toml declares the tested\nMSRV. Cargo.lock is committed; CI uses --locked. Unit preferences are presentation settings,\nnot a reason to erase source quantities. Keep core calculations independent of HTTP/storage.\n\n## Local gate\n```sh\ncargo fmt --all --check\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings\ncargo nextest run --workspace --locked\ncargo build --release --locked\ncargo deny check licenses\ncargo audit\nRUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked\ncargo msrv verify -- cargo check --all-targets --locked\n```\nInstall cargo-nextest, cargo-deny, cargo-audit and cargo-msrv if absent. CI additionally\nuses cargo-llvm-cov and cargo-sbom. Tests may unwrap assertion setup; production may not.\n\n## Workflows\n- CI: fmt/clippy, nextest/coverage, MSRV, debug/release artifacts, SPDX SBOM and size metrics.\n- Security audit: `RustSec` advisory checks and dependency licence policy; runs daily as well.\n- Docs: strict rustdoc with requirements/specs/ADRs embedded, uploaded and deployed to Pages.\n- Renovate: daily self-hosted Renovate using `RENOVATE_TOKEN` (existing repository secret).\n\nAll workflows support `workflow_dispatch`. GitHub Pages must use the GitHub Actions build\nsource. Workflow permissions are scoped to the jobs that publish or create audit issues.\nNo upstream advisory ignores, ESP targets or machine-specific paths are retained.\nTo repeat a run: `gh workflow run <file>.yml --ref main --repo Th3Link/mealshop`.\nInspect `gh run list` and failed job logs; a dispatched workflow is not evidence of success.\n\n## Documentation\n`src/docs.rs` embeds the Markdown sources as rustdoc modules. Run `cargo doc --no-deps` and\nopen `target/doc/mealshop_server/docs/index.html`. The Docs workflow adds a root landing\npage. After adding a spec or ADR, update its index; docs generation discovers Markdown files.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_guides_development_md {}

#[doc = "# Bootstrap provenance\n\nRetrieved 2026-11-07:\n- [curvyo/curvyo](https://github.com/curvyo/curvyo/tree/9ca3ebba86e511cd24559424f13fa2183caeea57):\n  AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md conventions, specs/README.md lifecycle, docs/adr format and AGPL text.\n  Mealshop rewrites project-specific guidance; no Curvyo product modules or agent setup copied.\n- [Th3Link/homeautomation](https://github.com/Th3Link/homeautomation/tree/4c65a45d2046d795aaef5b79e3c311ae1f0a1847):\n  CI quality gate, nextest/coverage, cargo-msrv, debug/release build artifacts, cargo-sbom,\n  cargo-deny/audit, self-hosted Renovate and rustdoc/Pages publication patterns.\n  ESP/QEMU/firmware jobs do not apply. Metrics measure host server binary bytes, not ESP memory.\n  No upstream advisory exceptions or hardware-specific Renovate exclusions are carried over.\n\nThe initial customer request authorizes bootstrap and direct main publication. Future feature\nspecs remain Draft; they are not completed just because their documentation exists.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_provenance_md {}

#[doc = "# Product requirements\n\nOrigin: customer vision, 2026-11-07. Mealshop is a working name.\nThe [feature index](../page_specs_readme_md/index.html) maps F01–F20 one-to-one to acceptance contracts.\n\n## Cross-cutting requirements\n- N01: Rust/Axum/Tokio backend and Flutter client; standalone and free Nextcloud `ExApp` deployment.\n- N02: Selectable Git/file, PostgreSQL, SQLite or MariaDB persistence, with portable versioned data.\n- N03: Precise quantities, configurable presentation, reproducible nutrition and explicit unknowns.\n- N04: Household isolation, dietary exclusions above recommendations, consented calendar/learning use.\n- N05: AGPL-3.0-only complete software; paid official app, self-build allowed, free/paid hosted tiers.\n- N06: Imported recipes share their source URL only, including via collections, MCP and federation.\n- N07: Multi-day processes and reminders survive restart and explain delivery limitations.\n- N08: Spec-driven development, ADRs and CI with Renovate, builds, docs/Pages, audit, SBOM, metrics and MSRV.\n\n## Scope and unresolved decisions\nM0 implements the bootstrap only. Nutrition data provider/licences, identity/authentication,\ncalendar provider, database migration/sync details, payment provider, attestation feasibility,\nnotification transport, federation protocol and concrete paid tiers remain open. No customer\nprice, health guarantee or provider commitment is inferred from the vision.\n\n## Traceability\nN01 → F01/F18; N02 → F18; N03 → F02/F03/F04; N04 → F09/F10/F11;\nN05 → F19; N06 → F05/F16/F17/F20; N07 → F12/F13/F14; N08 → F01.\nEach feature plan must link its tests to its numbered acceptance criteria before Done.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_requirements_md {}

#[doc = "# Roadmap\n\nThis is a proposed delivery order, not a promise of dates. Dependencies can change after review.\n\n| Milestone | Outcome | Features |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Runnable server, specs, docs and delivery pipeline | F01 |\n| M1 | Recipe/nutrition foundation, household constraints, first storage/deployment slice | F02–F04, F09, F18 |\n| M2 | Shared recipes, family plans, shopping, guided cooking, incremental preference feedback | F05–F07, F10–F12 |\n| M3 | Barcode, long dough processes, inventory/offers, imports, MCP | F08, F13, F15–F17 |\n| M4 | Brewing/fermentation and commercial operations | F14, F19 |\n| M5 | Opt-in federation | F20 |\n\nBefore M1, choose the first persistence adapter and identity model, validate nutrient data\nsources, and specify the Flutter interaction. F18 spans several milestones: a first backend\nis not completion of the four-backend/Nextcloud/client acceptance contract. Online learning\nstarts with inspectable rules and feedback; production ML follows measured benefit.\n"]
pub mod page_docs_roadmap_md {}

